
=== DuckDB

Use `symadmin module install duckdb` to install driver files, or copy your own files into the `lib` sub-directory.

DuckDB is an embedded, in-process analytical database. SymmetricDS supports DuckDB as a target platform where data
can be loaded, but it does not support data capture because DuckDB does not support triggers.

See <<Write-Only Node>> for details on setting up a write-only node in SymmetricDS.

In the engine properties file, set the following properties:
----
load.only=true
target.db.driver=org.duckdb.DuckDBDriver
target.db.url=jdbc:duckdb:/path/to/database.db
target.db.user=
target.db.password=
----

If a table has a primary key or unique index, DuckDB rejects rows with duplicate keys. Before inserting a row,
SymmetricDS checks whether a row with the same key already exists. If it does, the row is not inserted, and it is
handled as a conflict using the conflict resolution settings for the table, such as fallback to update. Foreign keys
are not created on DuckDB tables because DuckDB does not support adding them with ALTER TABLE. Auto increment columns are
created with a sequence and a default value that calls nextval() on that sequence.

Character types (char, varchar, nchar, nvarchar, and clob) are created as varchar without a size. Binary types are
created as blob. Float is created as double, and the maximum precision for decimal and numeric is 38.
